* =========================================================================
* PTAT bias block for the EML fabric (2026-07-23).
*
* Principle: I_UNIT is PTAT: iu = dVBE/R_ptat = nvt*ln(8)/R_ptat.
* Cell resistors RU = RLN = nvt/iu => RU/R_ptat = 1/ln(8): pure ratio.
* => u*iu*RU = u*nvt(T) exactly; ln V->I gain likewise => the cell is
* temperature-invariant IN ITS OWN UNITS to first order. The absolute
* unit current drifts with R tempco -- the system is ratiometric
* (MDACs, readout all reference the same master).
*
* iu = 0.5 uA at 300 K. Core runs 4 units (2 uA/leg): R_ptat =
* nvt*ln8/2u = 27.95k. Distribution: PMOS legs on the pbias line,
* W ratio = current ratio (diode leg W=8 <=> 2 uA).
* Startup: 10M bleed on pbias (pulls gate low, wakes the dVBE loop);
* constant ~85 nA systematic offset on the diode leg -- absorbed, and
* replaceable by an active startup at layout time.
* Rails: resistor divider (10 uA) + followers. VE must SINK up to
* ~20 uA of emitter current -> ota2-based follower (NMOS CS output).
* =========================================================================

.subckt ptatbias vdd pbias nd12 nd055 vcasc vgu vg4 vg16
* --- dVBE core: QP1 1x diode; QP2 8x degenerated by R_ptat ---
XMPP1 nb  pbias vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 W=16 L=8
XMPP2 pbias pbias vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 W=16 L=8
XQP1 nb nb 0 0 sky130_fd_pr__npn_05v5_W1p00L1p00
* 8x emitter area as 4 x W1p00L2p00 (2 um^2 each): the PDK only ships
* ngspice models for the 1x and 2x geometries, and each NPN needs 6.3 um
* of dnwell spacing, so 4 devices instead of 8 halves the bias-slot width.
XQP2A pbias nb ne2 0 sky130_fd_pr__npn_05v5_W1p00L2p00
XQP2B pbias nb ne2 0 sky130_fd_pr__npn_05v5_W1p00L2p00
XQP2C pbias nb ne2 0 sky130_fd_pr__npn_05v5_W1p00L2p00
XQP2D pbias nb ne2 0 sky130_fd_pr__npn_05v5_W1p00L2p00
* 30k = 6 x 5k segments, matching the layout grid (was 28.8k, which
* is not an integral number of 5k segments)
* 30k here is the NOMINAL TRIM SETTING, not a fixed resistor.  The silicon
* implements R_ptat as bias/rptat_trim.inc (15k + shorted 5k/10k/20k),
* which reads 30k at code t2t1t0 = 100.  This deck keeps the flat value so
* the chain simulation stays on the design point; sweep the codes with
* bias/rptat_trim_test.spice.
RPTAT ne2 0 30k
* startup: cap kick (charge only during ramp; no static error) +
* pseudo-resistor leaker (4x diode-connected PMOS, nA-class) as the
* DC escape guarantee. A 50M poly resistor would be 54 mm — silicon
* startup must be device-based.
CST vdd nb 1p
XSL1 nsl1 nsl1 pbias vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 W=0.42 L=8
XSL2 nsl2 nsl2 nsl1 vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 W=0.42 L=8
XSL3 nsl3 nsl3 nsl2 vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 W=0.42 L=8
XSL4 nd12 nd12x nsl3 vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 W=0.42 L=8
VSLS nd12x nd12 0

* --- rails: 330k divider (10 uA) + followers ---
* The 65k middle leg is split so the MDAC cascode bias falls out of the
* SAME divider: 85k from ground is 0.850 V, which is the value the weight
* DACs need (measured -- at 1.0 V the fine digits collapse above ~1 uA of
* input current, at 1.55 V they deliver zero).  Taps from ground:
*   55k -> 0.550 (ve)   85k -> 0.850 (vcasc)   120k -> 1.200 (vrefb)
RD1 vdd nd12 210k
RD2A nd12 vcasc 35k
RD2B vcasc nd055 30k
RD3 nd055 0 55k
* vcasc drives ~130 cascode gates and sinks no DC current, but it is a
* high-impedance tap (85k) -- decouple it locally.
CVC vcasc 0 2p
* rail taps nd12 / nd055 leave the block unbuffered -> see raildrv

* --- unit reference for the weight DACs ---
* pbias is the gate of the CORE legs (W=16 L=8, W/L=2, 2 uA).  An MDAC
* unit device is W=8 L=2 -- W/L=4 -- so gating it from pbias directly
* gives 4.4 uA, not the 0.5 uA that "one unit" means: every alpha weight
* would have been 8.9x too strong.  Generate a proper unit gate instead:
* a W/L=0.5 leg pulls 0.5 uA off pbias, an NMOS mirror turns it around,
* and a W=8 L=2 PMOS diode carrying it defines vgu -- so an identical
* device on vgu carries exactly one unit by construction.
XREFP  nref pbias vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 W=4 L=8
XREFN  nref nref  0   0   sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 W=8 L=2
XREFM  vgu  nref  0   0   sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 W=8 L=2
XREFPDs nrpd vgu   vdd  vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 W=8 L=2
XREFPDc vgu  vcasc nrpd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 W=8 L=1

* --- shared MDAC reference divider ---
* Every ALPHA weight on the chip takes its reference from pbias, so the
* /4 and /16 gates are generated ONCE here rather than per weight (each
* chain is 18 devices; six copies would be pure waste).  Gamma weights
* are multiplying and keep their own chains.
XDIV4  vgu   vg4  vcasc vdd 0 mdac_div
XDIV16 vg4   vg16 vcasc vdd 0 mdac_div
.ends

* Rail drivers + decoupling: TOP-LEVEL block. The buffers are ota2b
* instances (39.7 x 72.8 um each) and the decaps are 50 um square, so
* neither fits the 34 um bias strip; they are placed with the cell array
* instead. Electrically identical to having them inside ptatbias.
* ONE buffer, on ve only, and NO decap -- every choice below is measured
* (bias/ve_load.spice, raildrv_load.spice, raildrv_stab.spice, 2026-07-29):
*   i(ve) = 23.54 uA vs i(vrefb) = -70.8 nA, a factor of 330.  vrefb is
*   four OTA gates + four bleed resistors; on the bare divider it settles
*   at 1194.6 mV and the cell's 2.83 pA/mV sensitivity makes that -5.4 mV
*   worth 0.0025% of output -- a thousandth of the chain's 0.0027-rms
*   accuracy.  Buffer the rail that carries current, not the one that
*   does not: only ONE ota2b site exists on the die.
*   The old CVE/CVRB 5p decaps were ADDING a pole -- the step response is
*   bit-identical from 500 fF to 1 fF because ota2b's internal CC is what
*   compensates.  ~4.9 kum2 of MiM plate deleted.
* Port order matches lvsref/raildrv.spice.
.subckt raildrv ve nd055 vdd pbias
XBUF2 ve nd055 ve vdd pbias ota2b
.ends

* (legacy) Rail decoupling (5 pF each = 2500 um^2): TOP-LEVEL devices, not part of
* the bias block -- they belong near the consumers and would otherwise
* consume 89% of the bias slot. Instantiate once per chip.
